course: dictionary
lesson: 4794
title: Humble: not thinking you are better
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, so the context tells you which one to use. «The wise moves: ask, don't assume; discuss ideas, never insult people; ... and hold your own beliefs with care, staying humble and curious.» Here humble means not proud, not thinking you are better than other people.
explain: «Pau Amma gets his hard shell back for eleven months of the year, but in the twelfth month it will go soft again, to keep him humble.» The clue is the deal: the magician wants to stop Pau Amma getting too proud. So humble means not proud here.
explain: «The small team humbled the champions.» Now humble is a verb, a doing word. The clue is that a small team beat a big champion, so humbled means made the champions less proud, or beat them. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
fact: «Humble» means not proud, not thinking you are better or more important than other people.
fact: «Humble» can also mean simple or poor, as in «a humble cottage» or «from humble beginnings».
fact: As a verb, «humble» means to make someone feel less proud, or to beat a strong opponent.
fact: «In my humble opinion» is a polite way to share your view, without bragging.
fact: «Eat humble pie» means to admit you were wrong.
exercise: «The Magician makes a deal: Pau Amma gets his hard shell back, but it will go soft again to keep him humble.» What does humble mean here? | Too tired to move | Hungry and cold | Very rich and famous | *Less proud, so he does not boast
exercise: «The small team humbled the champions.» What does humbled mean? | Cheered for | *Beat a strong team and made them less proud | Forgot | Copied
exercise: «They came from humble beginnings.» Find and copy the word that means simple or poor. | from | beginnings | they | *humble
test: «In my humble opinion, the film was great.» What does humble mean here? | Shy and quiet | *Polite, a modest way to share your view | Bored and sleepy | Very angry
test: Which sentence shows someone being humble? | *Mia said, «I was wrong, and I'm sorry. Can you help me put it right?» | Mia said, «Nobody can beat me.» | Mia said, «I am the best at everything.»
exam: What does humble mean in «She stayed humble after winning the race»? | Poor and hungry | Very angry | *Not proud, not boasting about winning | Very loud
